+More is true. Filling each dotted cusp of the link exterior along its zero slope gives the exterior of the five framed attaching circles in $\#_3(S^1\times S^2)$. For Figure 2 and its first drawing, these five-cusped exteriors each have 572 connected 3-fold covers, and the multisets of their first homology groups differ. For Figure 1 and its first drawing, the 31 connected double covers already differ. The covers are enumerated combinatorially and their homology is computed exactly, so no homeomorphism of $\#_3(S^1\times S^2)$ carries one family of attaching circles to the other. In particular, the two versions are not related by an isotopy in the boundary of the 1-handlebody, with any choice of basis, or by 1-handle slides. None of this obstructs a slide of one 2-handle over another. As the third author observed, a single such slide relates the two diagrams.
 
